        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: explain pull request automation workflow",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw contributors see Barnacle and ClawSweeper labels, comments, queue delays, proof requests, and re-review requests after opening a PR, but the contributor-facing workflow is not summarized in one OpenClaw docs page.\n\nCloses #101172.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a practical pull request workflow guide for new contributors. It explains:\n\n- what Barnacle does;\n- what ClawSweeper does;\n- how to ask ClawSweeper for another review;\n- what `status: ⏳ waiting on author` means;\n- what evidence/proof is useful;\n- why proof redaction is the contributor's responsibility;\n- why ClawSweeper may not respond immediately;\n- how to troubleshoot and when to ask in `#clawtributors`.\n\nIt also adds a small `CONTRIBUTING.md` pointer and includes links to the ClawSweeper repo/docs for people or organizations that want to fork similar automation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNew contributors have a single place to understand the post-PR workflow instead of inferring it from bot comments, labels, Discord, and scattered docs.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidation run locally:\n\n```text\npnpm docs:check-mdx\npnpm docs:check-links\npnpm docs:map:check\npnpm format:docs:check\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nAll passed.\n\n## Review request\n\n@clawsweeper review\n\nClawSweeper: because this page documents Barnacle and ClawSweeper behavior, please suggest any additions, corrections, or wording changes that would make the workflow clearer or more accurate for new contributors.\n",
